      "code": {
        "pseudo": "Hero, first second: <video> plays the clip. Each frame, read video.currentTime,\npick the recorded skeleton frame for that time, draw it on a <canvas> on top.\nNo model, no wasm before the hero moves.\n\nPlayground: the worker and model start when the section scrolls into view\nor when Try it live is pressed. Then the hero can switch to real results too.\n\nLook and motion, on every section:\n- Custom SVG icons drawn for this site (joint, angle, rule, replay, camera, mask...), no icon pack.\n- Sections and cards fade and rise in as they scroll into view (IntersectionObserver + CSS).\n- Small SVG animations: the skeleton draws its lines in, angle arcs sweep, a rule check ticks.\n- All motion turns off under prefers-reduced-motion.",
        "docs": "// MediaPipe Pose Landmarker web guide (ai.google.dev/edge/mediapipe)\nconst vision = await FilesetResolver.forVisionTasks(\n  \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@mediapipe/tasks-vision@latest/wasm\"\n);\nconst poseLandmarker = await PoseLandmarker.createFromOptions(vision, {\n  baseOptions: {\n    modelAssetPath: \"pose_landmarker_full.task\",\n    delegate: \"GPU\"\n  },\n  runningMode: \"VIDEO\"\n});\nposeLandmarker.detectForVideo(video, performance.now(), (result) => {\n  for (const landmarks of result.landmarks) {\n    drawingUtils.drawConnectors(landmarks, PoseLandmarker.POSE_CONNECTIONS);\n  }\n});\n// The site keeps serving the wasm and model from its own folder (CSP: connect-src 'self')."
      }
    },
